[[8,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Undo the bolt (1a) and remove the single drive belt tensioner\n(1b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2052788.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[8,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>1. Place the engine components single drive belt moving tensioner\n(1a) back in its housing and fix it tightening the bolt (1b) to\nthe recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>SINGLE SERVICES MOBILE BELT TENSIONER</p></td><td><p>M10</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Upper engine crankcase side) 4.5 ÷ 5.5</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2052789.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]]